    <p class="label red" style="margin:0 0 20px">A common story</p>
    <h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.5vw,60px);margin:0">A website should work as hard as your marketing.</h2>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">A store spends on ads and SEO. The traffic arrives. Then the site is slow on a phone, the checkout is unclear, and a plugin update breaks a page nobody has checked since launch. Nobody is sure who to ask, so the problem sits there.</p>
    <p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">That gap is where most ecommerce website work starts. We treat design, development, conversion, speed and upkeep as one job, not five separate invoices, so the site keeps up with the search traffic you are paying for.</p>
    <p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0;color:var(--ink)">You get one team, one plan, and a price agreed before any work starts.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>
